{
  "_about": "Karl's sound effects, sorted by what they are for (judged from their waveforms and measurements: sfx_index.py). licence: pixabay = Pixabay Content License, free for commercial use without attribution; karl = Karl's own motion-design pack (October 2026, \"SFX pack 2\"), supplied by him for client films; cc0 = public domain (Kenney's Interface Sounds, kenney.nl, CC0 1.0), free for any use, no credit; apple = Apple's own system sounds, for reference and internal drafts only, never in a client delivery. character: how it feels, to match the film's motion identity.",
  "categories": {
    "tap": "a finger touching the screen, a button pressed, a selection: one short transient",
    "double-tap": "a two-part click: a toggle, a confirm, a pressed-and-released button",
    "pop": "something small appearing: a card, a pin, a bubble, a badge",
    "appear-rise": "something opening or growing: a panel, a sheet, a window, a reveal; pitch rises",
    "dismiss-fall": "something closing, leaving or switching off; pitch falls",
    "chime": "a message or notification arriving; tonal, with a ring",
    "success": "something done, confirmed, saved, paid; rising notes",
    "ticker": "a run of even ticks: counting, loading, a list or wheel scrolling, typing",
    "swipe": "something sliding or sent: a swipe, a send, a soft move",
    "camera": "a photo taken",
    "stinger": "a long tonal moment: a start-up, a logo; use sparingly",
    "whoosh": "something passing the camera: a move, a fly-past, a whip, a scene change; lands at its loudest moment",
    "riser": "a build into a reveal; lands at the end of the climb",
    "gear": "something mechanical turning: a dial, a wheel, a counter winding, a part fitting into a system, a process running",
    "money": "a payment, a sale, revenue: a cash register or coins; literal, so only where money is the subject",
    "data": "digital processing: data loading, collected, scanned or analysed; an AI thinking; a stream of blips",
    "glitch": "a digital glitch or flicker: a text glitch, a screen switching, a tech reveal",
    "error": "something wrong, rejected or failed: the problem beat (a red error, a declined card, a broken flow); soft, never harsh"
  },
